# Where the `@jsr` scope comes from. `@std/csv` is a JSR package (csv.ts reads
# a spreadsheet with it); deno takes it straight off jsr, and wrangler's esbuild
# resolves it as a FILE under this directory's node_modules, so npm has to be
# able to fetch it too. JSR publishes an npm-compatible build of every package
# on this registry, which is what `npm:@jsr/std__csv` in package.json names.
@jsr:registry=https://npm.jsr.io
